From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Scott Kidder <scott.kidder@discordapp.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 15:16:25 -0700
Subject: media: Gracefully handle discard overflow in AudioDiscardHelper

Negative Matroska DiscardPadding (surfaced as skip_samples side data)
can drive AudioDiscardHelper into two bad states:

1. frames_discarded_so_far > decoder_delay_ trips CHECK_LE in
   ProcessBuffers, killing the renderer (STATUS_BREAKPOINT). This is the
   mechanism of a publicly circulating WebM/Vorbis crasher validated
   against Chromium 148-155. Turn it into a graceful buffer drop, per
   the crbug.com/987121 precedent for reachable CHECKs in this file.

2. Unbounded discard_frames_ carry-over from large front skips on
   multiple packets can starve the pipeline of decoded output
   indefinitely (observed as a permanent renderer hang with a
   Lavf-muxed WebM carrying -21.35ms DiscardPadding on late audio
   packets). Cap carry-over at 30 seconds of audio.

Both paths are reachable only via malformed media; well-formed files
are unaffected.

Bug: 969195

diff --git a/media/base/audio_discard_helper.cc b/media/base/audio_discard_helper.cc
index 2222572e173109534ca8d6ab41f6b4fa45dcf6db..21fa8368cd8d17e4c8a36fea5b838c15c60deef0 100644
--- a/media/base/audio_discard_helper.cc
+++ b/media/base/audio_discard_helper.cc
@@ -149,7 +149,15 @@ bool AudioDiscardHelper::ProcessBuffers(const TimeInfo& time_info,
       // frames already discarded.
       const size_t frames_discarded_so_far =
           original_frame_count - decoded_buffer->frame_count();
-      CHECK_LE(frames_discarded_so_far, decoder_delay_);
+      // Corrupt or hostile containers can provide discard padding which
+      // discards more frames than the decoder delay allows. Drop the buffer
+      // instead of crashing the renderer (crbug.com/987121 precedent).
+      if (frames_discarded_so_far > decoder_delay_) {
+        DLOG(ERROR) << "Discarding " << frames_discarded_so_far
+                    << " frames exceeds decoder delay of " << decoder_delay_
+                    << "; dropping buffer.";
+        return false;
+      }
       discard_start -= frames_discarded_so_far;
     }
 
@@ -172,6 +180,17 @@ bool AudioDiscardHelper::ProcessBuffers(const TimeInfo& time_info,
     DCHECK(!discard_frames_);
     discard_frames_ = start_frames_to_discard - frames_to_discard;
 
+    // Corrupt containers can request absurd carry-over discards (e.g. large
+    // negative Matroska DiscardPadding on many packets) which would starve
+    // the pipeline of decoded output indefinitely. Cap carry-over at a
+    // generous bound of 30 seconds of audio.
+    const size_t max_carryover = static_cast<size_t>(sample_rate_) * 30u;
+    if (discard_frames_ > max_carryover) {
+      DLOG(ERROR) << "Capping excessive discard carry-over of "
+                  << discard_frames_ << " frames to " << max_carryover << ".";
+      discard_frames_ = max_carryover;
+    }
+
     DVLOG(1) << "Front discard of " << frames_to_discard << " out of "
              << decoded_frames << " frames starting at " << discard_start;
 
